calculate what you owe — before and after recalculation.

.why = Delaware's bill uses Authorized Shares Method. most solo founders qualify for Assumed Par Value Method, which is dramatically cheaper.

---

## Delaware's bill (Authorized Shares Method)

from your 0.gather.position.yield.md:

| field | value |
|-------|-------|
| tax due | $ |
| annual assessment | $ |
| authorized shares | |

this is calculated as:
- 5,000 shares or less: $175
- 5,001 - 10,000 shares: $250
- each additional 10,000 shares: +$85
- 10,000,000 shares = **$85,165.00**/year (computed, not approximated)
- 20,000,000 shares = **$170,165.00**/year
- 23,510,000 shares and above = **$200,000.00**/year, the statutory maximum

